// DISABLE_NATIVE: targetFamily=MINGW


// A dependency (lib) and its dependent (user) both export a top-level fun f() in package p,
// so both klibs record the same IdSignature (the IC log: "SPLITTING BATCH: user and lib share
// a top-level signature: p/f|...[0]"), and IdSignature carries no library identity.
//
// The IC pipeline deserializes the already-cached dependency lib with
// DeserializationStrategy.ONLY_DECLARATION_HEADERS before user's own files
// (linkKlibs.kt:202-206: isFullyCachedLibrary -> ONLY_DECLARATION_HEADERS), so lib's f is
// bound into the shared SymbolTable first; every reference to p.f in user's klib IR then
// resolves to lib's declaration, and user's own same-signature f is silently skipped by the
// isBound check in IrFileDeserializer.deserializeAllFileReachableTopLevel -- no diagnostic.
// user's per-file cache therefore bakes callF() calling lib's f (20): every IC flavor
// (clean, default, unbatched) prints 20. A non-IC link deserializes the same klibs lazily in
// reference order (main pulls user's o.kt first), so user's f wins there and it prints 10 --
// which is the declaration-site semantics: user's callF() must call user's own f. Same
// klibs, two different programs, differing only in -Xenable-incremental-compilation.
//
// This is the function flavor of KT-91126 ("[K/N] Inconsistent class resolution with and
// without caches for the same class in two libraries", a duplicate of the KT-81760 clashing
// declarations family); the KT-81760 fix (c526ca2b4078) only fingerprint-suffixed cached
// FUNCTION codegen symbols, so the IR-level misbinding still reproduces. The val flavor of
// the same family -- where the dependent's own cache build crashes outright -- is pinned by
// the sibling test clashingValTwinCrashesDependentCacheBuild.

MODULES: lib, user, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib, user, main
